  "claim_rule": "Phase 8 establishes bounded reference framing and resilience contracts for WebSocket, QUIC, Unix/local IPC, offline/sneakernet and store-forward delivery. NAT and relay metadata cannot weaken authenticated identity or create trust; resource/partition/key-compromise drills are deterministic; archive compatibility preserves historical bytes and identities; and Holodeck sandbox invariants remain transport-independent. These are reference transport profiles, not a production-networking or deployed-interoperability claim.",
  "promotion_requirements": {
    "interoperable_federation": "requires a later deployed multi-node interoperability profile across independently operated nodes and admitted transports",
    "production_networking": "requires production socket backends, deployment hardening, operational evidence, abuse controls and independent review",
    "remote_execution": "not admitted by the current constitutional posture",
    "host_level_sandbox": "requires separately reviewed host/VM/container/hypervisor isolation",
    "oracle_holodeck_synthetic_admission": "requires a separate reviewed synthetic non-evidence input contract"
